	(text "PWM GATING + 5 V INPUT LEVEL (FAST PATH)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 437.626 114.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0dd113a6-23c7-5f75-995c-f210a6db633d")
	)
	(text "PWMk = PWMk_RX AND EN_DRV, EN_GD = EN_DRV, both at +5V: the NSI6651 input thresholds are specified at\nVCC1 = 5 V only (VINH <= 3.5 V, p7), so VCC1 = +5V and the AHCT gates (VIH 2.0 V) lift the 3.3 V logic.\nA trip removes the commands within ~20 ns, ahead of the RST/EN filter (0.48-0.8 us). +5V or +3V3 absent:\nEN_DRV / PWMk pulled down, AHCT unpowered -> 0, NSI6651 VCC1 UVLO -> OUT low (functional modes p28)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 437.626 194.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3fa72b5b-4aed-5275-8506-d2632fc2f508")
	)
	(text "A = PWMk_P, B = PWMk_N. 470R P->GND, 470R N->3V3, 120R across: an open, unplugged or unpowered pair reads\n-0.30 V / -0.29 V worst case (< VIT- -0.2 V) -> output LOW = gate off. The receiver's own open-input\nfail-safe (output HIGH) never applies: the bias always defines the pair. Driven high: 1.9 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 101.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "42601e7c-5523-50c7-b13d-6e211a68a959")
	)
	(text "FAIL-SAFE OFF: THE THREE LOSS CASES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 323.62 114.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5e983721-98e5-505a-9902-e99f88f74d3b")
	)
	(text "FLT DRIVER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 316.832 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "72358ff8-db62-51a9-85c8-f9a03e8f911a")
	)
	(text "Same bias: open EN = LOW = drivers disabled. Spare receivers: A low, B high."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.392 76.612 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "81c73330-3df2-5a52-a7ce-6e8b459dd20a")
	)
	(text "PRE_N = OCP_OK AND OCN_OK AND OT_WIN_OK (low on fault) sets the latch: FAULT_N low until EN drops; with EN\nlow AND a fault still present both /PRE and /CLR are low (Q = /Q = H, Table 8-1), so FLT_OK = DRV_FLT_N AND\nRDY AND FAULT_N AND PRE_N reports the LIVE fault too (PVR-07 / INT-17); EN rising re-sets the latch.\nEN_DRV = EN_RX AND RDY AND FAULT_N drives every RST/EN. RDY (wired-AND: drivers, bias PG, +24V and +15V\nmonitors) reaches the CELL pin through a push-pull SN74LVC1G17: actively high when ready, low otherwise;\nunpowered = Ioff, the card's 100 k pull-down reads not ready (INT-14)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 214 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9e229f42-861c-5af3-8d3b-e789cf836b8f")
	)
	(text "EN RECEIVER (FAIL-SAFE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.392 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9f298ca4-b1a9-598a-8ec0-d3729355f4a3")
	)
	(text "FAULT LATCH, GATE ENABLE, FLT, RDY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 114.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ab42e436-912f-509e-be4c-12aeec4c9001")
	)
	(text "FLT_P = FLT_OK, FLT_N = /FLT_OK. CTRL receives the pair swapped with its own bias: healthy = -2 V\n= no fault; this board unpowered = AM26LV31E outputs Hi-Z (SLLS848C) -> CTRL bias -> fault."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 316.832 68.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b8b3dab0-1f41-5f1e-b8c2-ba09d2bbd77c")
	)
	(text "PWM1-4 RECEIVERS (FAIL-SAFE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f12b09fb-d47a-5d97-8737-0beded800c96")
	)
	(text "1 CABLE UNPLUGGED: no +24V -> no gate bias, no logic: every gate sits at 0 V on its 10k gate-source resistor\n  (VGS(th) >= 1.9 V). With +24V still present, an open pair reads -0.30 V -> PWM and EN LOW.\n2 CTRL UNPOWERED, or rev C card not enabling (it tri-states its PWM/EN drivers unless CHB_OK, its enable and\n  our RDY are high, INT-15): driver outputs Hi-Z (<= 100 uA, SLLS848C p5) -> -0.29 V -> LOW. In reset the card\n  drives 0 (10k on its ePWM balls, EN = GATE_EN AND CHB_OK AND MCU enable).\n3 +3V3 ABSENT: LVC/AM26 Ioff -> 10k pull-downs hold EN_DRV low -> AHCT: EN_GD, PWMk low; RDY_CELL Hi-Z -> card\n  reads 0 V; FLT Hi-Z = fault. +5V ABSENT: NSI6651 VCC1 UVLO -> OUT low (p28), UCC14241-Q1 ENA = 0 -> bias off,\n  RDY / DRV_FLT_N lose their pull-ups (to +5V) -> not ready / fault. +24V REMOVED (D-012 channel B): RDY low at\n  >= 19.7 V -> EN_DRV and PWM low while bias regulates."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 323.62 165.204 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fb6b39c3-e6a7-5962-9c93-364faa95c944")
	)
